    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that \\(\\tan x = 2\\), we need to find \\(\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right)\\).\n\nWe use the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan(a + b) = \\frac{\\tan a + \\tan b}{1 - \\tan a \\tan b}\n\\]\n\nLet \\(a = x\\) and \\(b = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\). Knowing that \\(\\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4} = 1\\), we substitute into the formula:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}{1 - \\tan x \\tan \\frac{\\pi}{4}}\n\\]\n\nPlugging in the values:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{2 + 1}{1 - 2 \\cdot 1}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the numerator:\n\\[\n2 + 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nSimplify the denominator:\n\\[\n1 - 2 \\cdot 1 = 1 - 2 = -1\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( x + \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = \\frac{3}{-1} = -3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-3}\n\\]",
